    mlips:targetMaterial entity:mat-dimer-AA-ji2025 ;
    mlips:hasAccuracyMetric entity:metric-sog-AA-1-ji2025 .

entity:metric-sog-AA-1-ji2025 a mlips:AccuracyMetric ;
    rdfs:label "RMSE on forces over the whole data set: SOG-Net, AA dimers (short-range-only model: 1.13)" ;
    mlips:metricType mlips:RMSE ;
    mlips:metricProperty mlips:ForceProperty ;
    mlips:metricValue "0.06"^^xsd:double ;
    mlips:hasUnit mlips:MilliEV-PER-ANGSTROM .

###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The force RMSEs are stated 'across the whole dataset' (training and test together). The short-range-only comparison models (64.3 / 35.4 / 32.0 / 26.8 / 2.26 / 1.13 meV/A for CC / CP / PP / CA / PA / AA) are in the metric labels but not encoded as runs: they use the paper's own core-shell short-range network without the long-range layer, which has no registry method. Energy RMSEs are only in figure insets.
# - N_FFT is printed as '313', read as 31 grid points per dimension (31^3); worth a check against the PDF.
# - Not encoded: the toy NaCl electrolyte (Coulomb + Lennard-Jones reference, up to 4000 training configurations), molten bulk NaCl (Table S1, percentage errors), Table I (SOG-Net against CC-ACE, 4G-HDNNP and CACE-LR on charged systems, with a CACE short-range part), the polar dipeptide (Table S2) and the liquid-water tests; their values were not read.
# - The registry now has entity:SOG-Net (this paper) and entity:CACE-SOG (ji2026, the same long-range layer on a CACE short-range model); schema 0.1.2 cannot relate them.
# - The manifest classes this paper as 'Application/model instance'; it is a method paper. The DOI 10.1103/ssp9-7s81 is the Physical Review Letters DOI.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
